= P3D Export =

#type: node
#context: sop
#internal: a3ob_p3d_export
#tags: arma, p3d

"""Checks a P3D geometry or a LOD geometry like Validate and writes it as a .p3d file when Save to Disk is pressed. The output is the input."""

This node is the end of a network. It checks the geometry the way Validate does and, when you press Save to Disk, writes a .p3d file you can use in Arma. The output is the same as the input, so you can keep working after it.

@inputs

P3D geometry or LOD geometry:
    Input 1.

@parameters

Output File:
    #id: file

    The .p3d file to write.

    Type: File path (can name a new file). Default: $HIP/$HIPNAME.p3d. Files: *.p3d.

Save to Disk:
    #id: save

    Check the input again and write the file. Nothing is written when there are errors.

    Type: Button.

Check:
    #id: check

    Type: Menu. Default: Every cook.

    Every cook:
        check whenever the node cooks.

    When saving:
        check only on Save to Disk (for large models).

Errors Show As:
    #id: errorlevel

    Type: Menu. Default: Error (stop here).

    Error (stop here):
        the node turns red and the nodes below it stop.

    Warning (keep geometry):
        the node turns yellow and the geometry keeps flowing; the text still starts with Error:. Saving stops on errors either way.

Warnings Count As Errors:
    #id: strict

    Treat every warning as an error. Off by default: a warning can be what you meant.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Duplicate LODs:
    #id: dupes

    What to do with a LOD whose type and resolution were already written: Fail, Skip the later one, or Ignore and write both.

    Type: Menu. Default: Fail.

    Fail:
        Sets this to Fail.

    Skip:
        Sets this to Skip.

    Ignore:
        Sets this to Ignore.

Max Messages:
    #id: maxmessages

    How many messages the node shows. The rest are counted in one line and listed in the console.

    Type: Whole number. Default: 25. Allowed: At least 1; no upper limit.

Preset:
    #id: preset

    A saved set of the options below: Lossless, Arma 3 release, or one you saved with the Project root and presets shelf tool. Pick one and press Apply. Choosing does not change anything by itself.

    Type: Menu. Default: Lossless.

    The choices are made when you open the menu, from the geometry or the settings.

Apply:
    #id: apply

    Fill the options below from the chosen preset. Project Root and Keep a .bak stay as they are.

    Type: Button.

Selection Mask:
    #id: selmask

    Which point groups become selections: names separated by spaces, * and ? match, ^ before a name leaves it out. Groups named in a3ob_tagg_order are always selections.

    Type: Text. Default: * ^__*.

Lowercase:
    #id: lowercase

    Write texture and material paths, selection names (so proxy paths too) and property names and values in lower case, as Object Builder does. Warns when two names become equal.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Relative Paths:
    #id: relpaths

    Strip the project root (or at least the drive letter) from texture, material and proxy paths.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Project Root:
    #id: projectroot

    Used with Relative Paths. Empty means the root from the shelf settings, or P:\ without one.

    Type: Text. Default: (empty).

Sort Sections:
    #id: sortsections

    Order the faces by texture and material, as Object Builder does. This changes the face order.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Sort LODs:
    #id: sortlods

    Write the LODs sorted by resolution. Off keeps your order.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Auto-Components:
    #id: autocomponents

    Geometry LODs without a component selection get one per connected piece.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Renumber Components:
    #id: renumber

    Rename every selection that starts with component and digits to component01, component02, ... in the order they are written, per LOD. The name is lowercased and any text after the digits is lost.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Translate Names to Czech:
    #id: czech

    Rename selections that have an English name from Object Builder's table (body becomes telo, weapon becomes zbran) to the Czech name the game uses. Whole name, any case. Warns when two selections end up equal.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Drop UVs:
    #id: dropuvs

    LODs of a type that does not use UVs (Geometry, Memory, Roadway, the fire and view geometry types) are written without UV sets and with zero face UVs, as Object Builder does. The geometry on the node is not changed.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Keep a .bak:
    #id: backup

    When a file is overwritten, keep the old one as .bak.

    Type: On or off. Default: Off.

Check LOD-Type Rules:
    #id: typerules

    Warn about what Object Builder's validator would: rules for geometry, shadow, roadway and other LOD types. Each rule has its own switch below.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-UV2: At most 2 UV sets:
    #id: t2uv2

    The LOD has no more than 2 UV sets.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-CONTIG: Contiguous mesh:
    #id: t2contig

    Geometry, shadow and underground LODs: no flipped polygons (shared edges run in opposite directions).

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-TRI: Triangulated:
    #id: t2tri

    Geometry, shadow and underground LODs: every polygon is a triangle.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-CONVEX: Convex mesh:
    #id: t2convex

    Geometry and underground LODs: every shared edge is convex or flat.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-COMP: Component selections:
    #id: t2comp

    Geometry and underground LODs: a group called component01, component02, ... exists.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-MASS: Mass is set:
    #id: t2mass

    Geometry LOD: the points have a total mass of at least 0.001.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-MASSALL: Every point has mass:
    #id: t2massall

    Geometry LOD: every point has a mass of at least 0.001.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-SHARP: No smooth edges:
    #id: t2sharp

    Shadow and underground LODs: with smooth polygons, every shared edge is in a3ob_sharp.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-NOMAT: No materials:
    #id: t2nomat

    Shadow and underground LODs: no polygon has a texture or material.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-SHADOWRES: Conventional shadow resolution:
    #id: t2shadowres

    Shadow LODs: the resolution is 0, 10, 1000, 1010 or 1020.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-SHADOWOFF: Shadow not disabled:
    #id: t2shadowoff

    Shadow LODs: no LODNoShadow = 1 property.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-PC-EDGE: No edges in point clouds:
    #id: t2pcedge

    Memory, land contact and hit-point LODs: no 2-point primitives.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-PC-FACE: No faces in point clouds:
    #id: t2pcface

    Memory, land contact and hit-point LODs: no polygons.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-RW-FACES: Has polygons:
    #id: t2rwfaces

    Roadway, ground layer and paths LODs: at least one polygon.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-RW-LIMIT: Roadway point limit:
    #id: t2rwlimit

    Roadway LODs: at most 255 points.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-RW-SOUND: Roadway sound textures:
    #id: t2rwsound

    Roadway LODs: every polygon has a texture (the sound).

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-GL-UV: Ground layer UV set:
    #id: t2gluv

    Ground layer LODs: exactly one UV set.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-GL-UVVALUES: Ground layer UV values:
    #id: t2gluvvalues

    Ground layer LODs: every UV is (0, 0), (1, 0), (1, 1) or (1, -1).

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-PATH-ENTRY: Path entry points:
    #id: t2pathentry

    Paths LODs: a group called in01, in02, ... exists.

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

T2-PATH-POS: Path position points:
    #id: t2pathpos

    Paths LODs: the same test as the entry rule (A3OB's own test, see spec 17.1.1).

    Type: On or off. Default: On.

The full page for this node is docs/user/reference/a3ob_p3d_export.html in the A3OB folder. Open it in a web browser.
